body:
Same issue in the alternate-type DB fallback: a single invalid `metadata` JSON payload will throw during `map()` and cause the method to return an empty list with the error swallowed by the outer catch. Handle JSON parse failures per record so other valid records are still returned/hydrated.
```suggestion
                        const hydratedItems: any[] = [];
                        for (const record of altRecords as any[]) {
                            let data = record.metadata;
                            if (typeof data === 'string') {
                                try {
                                    data = JSON.parse(data);
                                } catch {
                                    // Skip records with invalid JSON metadata, continue hydrating others
                                    continue;
                                }
                            }
                            SchemaRegistry.registerItem(request.type, data, 'name');
                            hydratedItems.push(data);
                        }
                        items = hydratedItems;
```
